{"id":"024b72650b2c1368","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-artin-wedderburn.md","title":"Artin–Wedderburn Theorem","display":"thm-artin-wedderburn — Artin–Wedderburn Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-artin-wedderburn","aliases":["58-thm-artin-wedderburn"],"display":"thm-artin-wedderburn — Artin–Wedderburn Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch11/58-df-ring.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-ring-homomorphism.md]]","[[58-df-bijective]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-artin-wedderburn"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-artin-wedderburn</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-artin-wedderburn — Artin–Wedderburn Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1c30d21ea7b443f6\" href=\"?note=1c30d21ea7b443f6\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-ring.md\">../batch11/58-df-ring.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"28f002080d71355a\" href=\"?note=28f002080d71355a\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-ring-homomorphism.md\">../batch09/58-df-ring-homomorphism.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"58-df-bijective\">58-df-bijective</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,I,J,D,+_D,\\cdot_D,0_D,1_D,D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet,k,S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S,f\\in V\">\\(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,I,J,D,+_D,\\cdot_D,0_D,1_D,D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet,k,S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S,f\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ring}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{Ring}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RingHom}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RingHom}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> are the imported structured predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SemisimpleRing}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SemisimpleRing}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DivisionRing}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{DivisionRing}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RingIso}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RingIso}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiniteMatrixProduct}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FiniteMatrixProduct}_S\\)</span> are defined below</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\prod_{i&lt;k}^{\\mathrm{Ring}}M_{n_i}(D_i,+_i,\\cdot_i,0_i,1_i)\">\\(\\prod_{i&lt;k}^{\\mathrm{Ring}}M_{n_i}(D_i,+_i,\\cdot_i,0_i,1_i)\\)</span> denotes the canonical set-coded finite product of matrix rings: matrices are functions <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n_i\\times n_i\\to D_i\">\\(n_i\\times n_i\\to D_i\\)</span>, and the ring operations are the usual entrywise sum and matrix product</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}left\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(I;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\land I\\subseteq R\\land0_R\\in I\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall a,b\\in I\\;(a-_Rb\\in I)\n\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall a\\in I\\;(r\\cdot_Ra\\in I).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}left\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(I;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\land I\\subseteq R\\land0_R\\in I\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall a,b\\in I\\;(a-_Rb\\in I)\n\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall a\\in I\\;(r\\cdot_Ra\\in I).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}semisimple\\text{-}ring\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SemisimpleRing}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\land0_R\\neq1_R\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall I\\subseteq R\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(I;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\to\n\\exists J\\subseteq R\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(J;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{10em}\\land I\\cap J=\\{0_R\\}\n\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\exists a\\in I\\;\\exists b\\in J\\;(r=a+_Rb)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}semisimple\\text{-}ring\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SemisimpleRing}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\land0_R\\neq1_R\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall I\\subseteq R\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(I;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\to\n\\exists J\\subseteq R\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(J;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{10em}\\land I\\cap J=\\{0_R\\}\n\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\exists a\\in I\\;\\exists b\\in J\\;(r=a+_Rb)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}division\\text{-}ring\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{DivisionRing}_S(D,+_D,\\cdot_D,0_D,1_D)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(D,+_D,\\cdot_D,0_D,1_D)\\land0_D\\neq1_D\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall a\\in D\\;\\bigl(a\\neq0_D\\to\n\\exists b\\in D\\;(a\\cdot_Db=1_D\\land b\\cdot_Da=1_D)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}division\\text{-}ring\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{DivisionRing}_S(D,+_D,\\cdot_D,0_D,1_D)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(D,+_D,\\cdot_D,0_D,1_D)\\land0_D\\neq1_D\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall a\\in D\\;\\bigl(a\\neq0_D\\to\n\\exists b\\in D\\;(a\\cdot_Db=1_D\\land b\\cdot_Da=1_D)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}ring\\text{-}iso\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{RingIso}_S(f;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R;S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathrm{RingHom}_S(f,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S)\n\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(f,R,S).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}ring\\text{-}iso\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{RingIso}_S(f;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R;S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathrm{RingHom}_S(f,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S)\n\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(f,R,S).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}finite\\text{-}matrix\\text{-}product\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{FiniteMatrixProduct}_S(S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S;k,D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\leftrightarrow\n\\langle S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S\\rangle\n=\\prod_{i&lt;k}^{\\mathrm{Ring}}M_{n_i}(D_i,+_i,\\cdot_i,0_i,1_i).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}finite\\text{-}matrix\\text{-}product\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{FiniteMatrixProduct}_S(S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S;k,D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\leftrightarrow\n\\langle S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S\\rangle\n=\\prod_{i&lt;k}^{\\mathrm{Ring}}M_{n_i}(D_i,+_i,\\cdot_i,0_i,1_i).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n&amp;\\mathrm{SemisimpleRing}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\exists k\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet,S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S,f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(D_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(D_\\bullet))\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(+_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(+_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\cdot_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(\\cdot_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(0_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(0_\\bullet))\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(1_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(1_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(n_\\bullet,k,\\omega_{&gt;0})\n\\land\\forall i&lt;k\\;\\mathrm{DivisionRing}_S(D_i,+_i,\\cdot_i,0_i,1_i)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{FiniteMatrixProduct}_S(S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S;k,D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{RingIso}_S(f;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R;S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn}\\vdash\n&amp;\\mathrm{SemisimpleRing}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\exists k\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet,S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S,f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(D_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(D_\\bullet))\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(+_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(+_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\cdot_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(\\cdot_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(0_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(0_\\bullet))\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(1_\\bullet,k,\\operatorname{ran}(1_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(n_\\bullet,k,\\omega_{&gt;0})\n\\land\\forall i&lt;k\\;\\mathrm{DivisionRing}_S(D_i,+_i,\\cdot_i,0_i,1_i)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{FiniteMatrixProduct}_S(S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S;k,D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{RingIso}_S(f;R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R;S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>All product length, matrix sizes, division-ring structures, product-ring data, and the isomorphism witness are quantified.</li>\n<li>Semisimplicity is tied to the displayed ring operations by the direct-complement condition on left ideals; it is no longer an undeclared carrier-only predicate that could choose unrelated operations.</li>\n<li>This is the structure theorem for semisimple rings.</li>\n<li>Wedderburn's theorem: finite division rings are fields.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch11/58-df-ring.md","status":"resolved","id":"1c30d21ea7b443f6","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-ring.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-ring-homomorphism.md","status":"resolved","id":"28f002080d71355a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-ring-homomorphism.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-bijective","status":"resolved","id":"d583890235faf0d5","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-bijective]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,I,J,D,+_D,\\cdot_D,0_D,1_D,D_\\bullet,+_\\bullet,\\cdot_\\bullet,0_\\bullet,1_\\bullet,n_\\bullet,k,S,+_S,\\cdot_S,0_S,1_S,f\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Ring}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RingHom}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Bijective}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SemisimpleRing}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DivisionRing}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RingIso}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FiniteMatrixProduct}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\prod_{i<k}^{\\mathrm{Ring}}M_{n_i}(D_i,+_i,\\cdot_i,0_i,1_i)","display":false},{"tex":"n_i\\times n_i\\to D_i","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}left\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}for\\text{-}artin\\text{-}wedderburn